{
  "an10.87:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 10.87 ",
  "an10.87:0.2": "9. Senior Mendicants ",
  "an10.87:0.3": "Disciplinary Issues ",
  "an10.87:1.1": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants concerning the mendicant Kalandaka: ",
  "an10.87:1.2": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "an10.87:1.3": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "an10.87:1.4": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "an10.87:2.1": "“Firstly, a mendicant raises disciplinary issues and doesn’t praise the settling of disciplinary issues. ",
  "an10.87:2.2": "This quality doesn’t conduce to fondness, respect, esteem, harmony, and unity. ",
  "an10.87:3.1": "Furthermore, a mendicant is not eager to train, and doesn’t praise taking up the training. … ",
  "an10.87:3.2": "",
  "an10.87:4.1": "Furthermore, a mendicant has corrupt wishes, and doesn’t praise getting rid of wishes. … ",
  "an10.87:4.2": "",
  "an10.87:5.1": "Furthermore, a mendicant is irritable, and doesn’t praise getting rid of anger. … ",
  "an10.87:5.2": "",
  "an10.87:6.1": "Furthermore, a mendicant denigrates others, and doesn’t praise getting rid of denigration. … ",
  "an10.87:6.2": "",
  "an10.87:7.1": "Furthermore, a mendicant is devious, and doesn’t praise getting rid of deviousness. … ",
  "an10.87:7.2": "",
  "an10.87:8.1": "Furthermore, a mendicant is deceitful, and doesn’t praise getting rid of deceitfulness. … ",
  "an10.87:8.2": "",
  "an10.87:9.1": "Furthermore, a mendicant doesn’t pay attention to the teachings, and doesn’t praise attending to the tea